# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Vercel deploy scope
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# This project has no build step: Vercel serves the repo root as static files,
# and vercel.json rewrites /api/* to the Cloudflare Worker. Without an ignore
# file Vercel uploaded the ENTIRE repository on every deploy - including test
# fixtures, docs, the Worker source and two legacy prototype folders.
#
# Measured before this file: ~79 MB per deployment. The Hobby plan allows
# 10 GB of deployment storage, so every ~126 deployments filled it.
#
# Nothing below is fetched by a served page. Verified: index / dashboard /
# quotation / portal / share / gallery / feedback-preview / oauth-complete
# contain zero href/src/url references to any of these directories.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Documentation and process notes (3.7 MB)
docs/
README.md
*.md

# Test suite, fixtures and screenshots (2.0 MB)
qa/

# Back end sources - the API lives on Cloudflare Workers, not here (1.2 MB)
platform/

# Legacy prototype folders, not linked from any served page (2.6 MB)
review/
concept-preview/

# Build/dev tooling
scripts/
.github/
node_modules/
**/node_modules/

# Local data and secrets - must never reach a static host
platform/data/
.env
.env.*
.dev.vars
.cf-vars

# Repo housekeeping
.gitignore
.assetsignore
.vercelignore
